Z||000000||AkursedX||09-05-2000||09:58 AM||||Hello all.  I have a 1988 Fiero GT that came from the factory with no rear wing and it got me to wonder....How many 88 Fiero GT's came without a rear wing.  I was just curious if anyone had an idea.  I like know these small types of useless information  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||09-05-2000||04:49 PM||||My t-top 88 did not have a spoiler. But the new owner wanted one- so I sold him the one off my car (bad idea)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sage||09-05-2000||06:47 PM||||I have a silver 86 GT that came from the factory without a wing.  A friend of mine has a gold 86 GT that also came with no wing from the factory.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Have a good one!<P>Sorry, I read the post wrong, thought you asked about ANY GT's without wings, not just 88's.  My mistake.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 09-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||pHoOl||09-05-2000||10:10 PM||||My 88 GT never had one.  you up to two for the count now?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||09-05-2000||10:38 PM||||well the wing didn't come with the GT package, it was an option.  The only car it came standard on was the Formula.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000005||My7Fieros||09-06-2000||02:05 PM||||I think the notchbacks look good without the wing (but they look better with), but I dont much care for the looks of a fastback without a wing...looks like its ass suffered from an allergic reaction to a bee sting.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfixit58||09-06-2000||04:01 PM||||I've had three GTs, 1-85 & 2-87s, none came from the factory with a wing.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||09-06-2000||10:30 PM||||There were exactly 5,300 '88GT's that came off the assembly line with a spoiler.<BR>861 had lumbar<BR>6,505 had PL<BR>614 with t-top<BR>3,226 with rear defog<BR>6,578 with a/c<BR>3,799 with 5-speed<BR>2,073 with sub-woofer<BR>66 with radio delete<BR>etc<BR>etc<BR>etc<P>Fiero Spotters Guide has all this and <B>much</B> more for just $5.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Black88GT||09-06-2000||11:04 PM||||I could never understand how people could order such worthless options as a crappy 25 watt paper subwoofer and a rear defog. (on a mid engined car - DUH!), and not order the spoiler!!  The GT looks naked without it IMO.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||5
Z||000009||Standard||09-07-2000||02:20 AM||||I think the fastback looks better without a wing, goes more with the sleek look.  It fits better into the more muscular look of the notchback, methinks.  <P>And the rear defog does actually help in the winter.  The window tends to fog up quick for the first 15 minutes of driving, because the window is still cold if you don't use the defog and the front manifold turns anywater that drips onto it into steam, which fogs up that window pretty quick.. I've found that the defog helps quite a bit.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000010||Black88GT||09-07-2000||04:25 PM||||Standard, the rear defog is not needed due to all the heat exhuded from the engine compartment.  I have had a totally iced out back window melt in less then 2 minutes due to the engine heat.  <P>||||reg||13
Z||000011||stimpy||09-07-2000||07:11 PM||||Uh-oh, I feel a defogger brawl coming on! hehehe...<BR>And now for something totally different. A wingless Fiero with a <B>rack?!</B><BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=258191&a=1921599&p=16712376&Sequence=0"> <P><BR>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 09-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||rockcrawl||09-07-2000||09:02 PM||||Stimpy, you forgot to mention that the racked wingless GT also has a rear defroster! Somebody's grandpa must have ordered that one!<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||12
Z||000013||Standard||09-07-2000||11:03 PM||||&lt;shrug&gt; I don't know about you, but I find it real helpful here in Minnesota during the winter.. I'm not saying you <B>have</B> to use it, I'm just saying I like to because I do notice a difference...  The rear window in my 84 with no rear defog has a tendency to fog up, and it gets pretty annoying.  These are just my own observations... results may vary, use at your own risk, etc etc...<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000014||Carrolles||09-08-2000||10:53 AM||||I like the rear defogger in my 85SE.  It clears up the fog on the glass so I can back out of my long driveway. True, it only takes a minute for the glass to clear up on it's own but I'm usually in a hurry.||||reg||1
